From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mountmgr: ask for UDisks2's own property changes only

Purpose: other programs' D-Bus signals no longer cost CPU time while UDisks2
runs (it is what mounts disc images for the XP shell, session/iso_mount.py).
Windows behavior: not applicable.
Wine before: the match rule for PropertiesChanged had no sender, so every
property change of any service on the system bus reached mountmgr.sys, and
for each one it fetched UDisks2's whole object tree (GetManagedObjects) to
look for the changed path. Without UDisks2 mountmgr drops the rule, so it
only shows where UDisks2 is installed.
Change: the rule asks for the signals of org.freedesktop.UDisks2 about block
devices, which are the only ones the filter acts on.
Evidence: on the EeePC (Atom N550) one ssh login made systemd send about 26
such signals; over 10 logins udisksd used 3.2 s of CPU time, dbus-daemon
1.3 s and winedevice.exe 0.57 s.
Scope: all programs; only the signals mountmgr receives change.
---
 dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c b/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c
index 99f37a3..09501fc 100644
--- a/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c
+++ b/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c
@@ -544,7 +544,9 @@ void run_dbus_loop(void)
                                                    "interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager',"
                                                    "path='/org/freedesktop/UDisks2'";
     static const char udisks2_match_properties[] = "type='signal',"
-                                                   "interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties'";
+                                                   "interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties',"
+                                                   "sender='org.freedesktop.UDisks2',"
+                                                   "path_namespace='/org/freedesktop/UDisks2/block_devices'";
 
 
     DBusError error;
